{#- CRITICAL: AGENT PERMISSIONS for the generated cluster. Two traps are encoded
    here and must survive any edit: `kubectl apply --dry-run` is spelled out as
    the two read-only values, because a bare `--dry-run=*` also matches
    `--dry-run=none` (kubectl's default — a live apply); and every destructive
    ZFS and rm form is denied in its `ssh <host> ...` wrapper as well as bare,
    because the storage host is reached over ssh, where a bare deny never matches. -#}
